From 31e7b81a1b4624278c84148d3fd44f1c32a8ec04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:20:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(face): recognise on both the colour and the IR camera
 (ir_recognition)

With a colour and an IR camera, Biopass recognised with one of them and
only checked that the IR camera saw some face, which a printed photo
can pass.

anti_spoofing.ir_recognition (default false): the IR camera recognises
too, against faces enrolled for it in faces-ir/ (next to faces/, which
the app lists and fills from the main camera). An attempt succeeds only
when the main (colour) camera and the IR camera both match, on frames at
most kBothCamerasMaxGap (2.5 s) apart, so matches from two moments or
attempts are never combined. It replaces the IR presence check; the AI
anti-spoofing model, when on, checks the colour frame. Faces must be
enrolled for both cameras, else face is unavailable, and ir_recognition
without an IR camera fails closed. When the IR camera is the main camera
it recognises already and nothing changes.

Cameras behind one capture pipeline stream one at a time: an attempt
starts on the camera that is open, closes it once a face (framed as
min_face_height asks) is found there and opens the other while the first
face is matched. The second camera stays open, so the next attempt
starts there and needs one switch, not two. Nothing falls back to one
camera: when the colour camera sees no face (a dark room, a covered
lens) the attempt fails.

FaceAuth takes test seams (enrolled faces, detection, matching, clock)
next to the camera opener; the debug log names the camera of each step.
Tests: face_both_cameras, config_validation, config_golden.
